                                        <p class="card-header">Treatment:</p>

                                        <p>
                                            Treatment and Management Strategies
                                            Supportive Care
                                            For the majority of patients who do not present with severe disease or identified risk factors for
                                            severe outcomes, the cornerstone of Mpox management involves supportive care aimed at
                                            alleviating symptoms and preventing complications. Clinical care protocols are designed to
                                            optimize patient comfort, manage potential complications, and mitigate long-term sequelae.
                                        </p>
                                        <div class="card-group">
                                            <b>
                                                Key
                                                components of supportive care include:
                                            </b>
                                            <ul>
                                                <li>Effective pain management through the administration of analgesics.</li>
                                                <li>
                                                    Diligent care for the rash, which may involve allowing lesions to air dry when feasible or
                                                    covering them with a moist dressing for protection as needed.
                                                </li>
                                                <li>
                                                    Strict avoidance of touching sores located in the mouth or eyes, with the judicious use of
                                                    mouth rinses and eye drops, while specifically avoiding cortisone-containing products.
                                                </li>
                                                <li>
                                                    Ensuring adequate hydration and nutrition to support overall recovery.
                                                </li>
                                                <li>
                                                    Proactive management and treatment of any secondary bacterial infections that may
                                                    arise.
                                                </li>
                                            </ul>
                                        </div>
